48ea3f82 (1549 1793434036948 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f407") (src . "languages: one ECMAScript function head, with export default and async\n\nThe javascript and typescript entries' function heads did not take\n`export default function f(`, and typescript's did not take `async`,\nso such a definition derived no name: an import with --symbols titled\nthe block by the editor's symbol name, and the title did not follow\nlater edits; an import without --symbols left the block unnamed. The\ntwo JSX entries landed with a wider head of their own.\n\nThe four entries that read JavaScript or TypeScript now share one\nstring, ecmascript-function-head, defined before the catalogue and\nunquoted into each entry's function-head slot: a declaration may be\nexported, exported as the default, and async, in that order. The\ntable literal is quasiquoted for it; the four unquotes are the only\nones in it. The entries cannot drift apart again.\n\nA definition head is also a cut for split-suggest: in TypeScript a\nline opening with `async function`, `export default function` or\n`export default async function` is now a cut, and in JavaScript a\nline opening with `export default function` is.\n\nREADME: the --symbols paragraph says which definitions derive no name\n(in TypeScript a class or a const; in JavaScript or TypeScript an\n`export default` of anything but a function).\n\nTests: text-heads gains a row per entry, each naming f from `export\ndefault function f`, `export async function f`, `async function f`\nand `export default async function f`; red on the base for javascript\nand typescript, green for the two JSX entries. No row baseline moves:\ntext-heads has no baseline line, and ecmascript-scan, the only fixture\nwhose corpus holds such heads, measures the same 110 rows and 124\nlines on the edit as on the base (its .tsx, .jsx and .js cases already\nhad them, and its one .ts case starts at offset 0).\n") (parent . root) (ord . 566))))
